  "narrative": "Raw-skeleton mode (today's default, no retrain) already classifies 92% of real (non-oracle, PoseNet-inferred) windows correctly across all 4 orientations, thanks to the orientation augmentation already baked into the synthetic training set (generate_sequence()'s orientation param, include_orientations=True). Rack-frame normalization scored 25% \u2014 WORSE, because the current LSTM checkpoint was never trained on rack-normalized features (a real distribution shift, not a bug). Recommendation: keep RACK_FRAME_NORMALIZE=False as the shipped default; the normalizer path is real and available, but needs a matched retrain (train/train_lstm.py with the flag on first) before it's a net improvement \u2014 exactly the 'retrain if needed' the build plan flagged."
